Query:
--Description:  For every collision that involves at least one motorcycle party,
--classify the crash as “helmet_used” if any motorcycle party shows the word
--“helmet” in either safety-equipment column; otherwise classify as “no_helmet”.
--Return the count of distinct collisions in each category.
SELECT
       CASE
         WHEN (p."party_safety_equipment_1" LIKE '%helmet%'
            OR p."party_safety_equipment_2" LIKE '%helmet%')
              THEN 'helmet_used'
         ELSE 'no_helmet'
       END                                 AS helmet_flag,
       COUNT(DISTINCT c."case_id")         AS collisions
FROM   "collisions" AS c
JOIN   "parties"     AS p
       ON c."case_id" = p."case_id"
WHERE  p."statewide_vehicle_type" LIKE '%motorcycle%'
GROUP  BY helmet_flag
LIMIT 20
Answer:
helmet_flag,collisions
helmet_used,19
no_helmet,9
Task: Please calculate the fatality rate for motorcycle collisions, separated by helmet usage. Specifically, calculate two percentages: 1) the percentage of motorcyclist fatalities in collisions where parties (drivers or passengers) were wearing helmets, and 2) the percentage of motorcyclist fatalities in collisions where parties were not wearing helmets. For each group, compute this by dividing the total number of motorcyclist fatalities by the total number of collisions involving that group. Use the parties table to determine helmet usage (from party_safety_equipment fields).

